menu "feckless_umode"

    config FECKLESS_UMODE_PREEMPTIBLE
        bool "Let interrupts land inside a U-mode window (experimental)"
        default n
        help
            By default a window raises the CLIC threshold to its maximum, so
            no interrupt is taken while the boxed program runs; they are
            serviced at the next syscall or exit.  Enabling this leaves the
            threshold alone and re-pends edge-triggered lines claimed by the
            private vector.  On an ESP32-P4 rev 1.3 Tab5 (u-feckless-0016)
            this stopped the tick on CPU0 and tripped the interrupt watchdog;
            leave it off unless investigating that.

endmenu
